=== lj-0: LEFT JOIN without WHERE (control) ===
== Query ==
SELECT p.grp, COUNT(*), COUNT(c.id), SUM(c.v)
FROM lj_parent AS p LEFT JOIN lj_child AS c ON c.id = p.id
GROUP BY p.grp;

Number of output lines, including header: 3

== Diff ==
==========



== Expected result ==
SELECT p.grp, COUNT(*), COUNT(c.id), SUM(c.v)
FROM lj_parent AS p LEFT JOIN lj_child AS c ON c.id = p.id
GROUP BY p.grp|
grp	COUNT(*)	COUNT(c.id)	SUM(c.v)
0	4	3	10
1	4	3	40

=== lj-1: LIKE on the right side rejects NULL (promoted to INNER) ===
== Query ==
SELECT p.grp, COUNT(*), SUM(c.v)
FROM lj_parent AS p LEFT JOIN lj_child AS c ON c.id = p.id
WHERE c.label LIKE 'a%'
GROUP BY p.grp;

Number of output lines, including header: 3

== Diff ==
==========



== Expected result ==
SELECT p.grp, COUNT(*), SUM(c.v)
FROM lj_parent AS p LEFT JOIN lj_child AS c ON c.id = p.id
WHERE c.label LIKE 'a%'
GROUP BY p.grp|
grp	COUNT(*)	SUM(c.v)
0	1	5
1	1	10

=== lj-2: NOT (col IS NULL) rejects NULL (promoted to INNER) ===
== Query ==
SELECT p.grp, COUNT(*), SUM(c.v)
FROM lj_parent AS p LEFT JOIN lj_child AS c ON c.id = p.id
WHERE NOT (c.v IS NULL)
GROUP BY p.grp;

Number of output lines, including header: 3

== Diff ==
==========



== Expected result ==
SELECT p.grp, COUNT(*), SUM(c.v)
FROM lj_parent AS p LEFT JOIN lj_child AS c ON c.id = p.id
WHERE NOT (c.v IS NULL)
GROUP BY p.grp|
grp	COUNT(*)	SUM(c.v)
0	2	10
1	2	40

=== lj-r1 (rejection): col IS NULL on the right side ===
WHERE condition on 'c' is not supported: 'c' is the right side of a LEFT JOIN and the condition can hold for its NULL-extended rows (as col IS NULL does). RonSQL would apply it as part of the join condition, keeping rows the WHERE should remove.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: WHERE on a LEFT JOIN's right side that holds for NULL is not supported.

